amd, radeonsi: include c99_alloca.h where alloca() is used.

These files call alloca() and rely on <stdlib.h> declaring it, as glibc's
does. illumos declares alloca() only in <alloca.h>, so they failed to
build ("implicit declaration of function 'alloca'"). Mesa's own
include/c99_alloca.h picks the right header per platform (<alloca.h> on
__sun); include it, as the rest of Mesa does. Upstreamable.

--- src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c.orig
+++ src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include "ac_surface.h"
 #include "ac_linux_drm.h"
 #include "util/u_sync_provider.h"
+#include "c99_alloca.h"
 
 #include "addrlib/src/amdgpu_asic_addr.h"
 #include "amd_family.h"
